# Structural Dynamics Checks

- State the engineering decision, objective, allowed choices, human judgment, and wrong-question trigger.
- Write quantity contracts before plots or checkers.
- State assumptions with values, units, sources, and sensitivity priority.
- Check units, axes, boundary conditions, and expected resonance/notch behavior.
- Use log frequency axes for frequency-domain plots unless the file explains why not.
- Show clean truth, observed data, absolute error, residuals, posterior/QOI samples, sensitivity, and reference comparison when applicable.

